IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 29/6/2026 to 20/10/2026" (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Part 13 Division 1 Subdivision (2) -- ss 249 to 252: expert and manager consents, the life of a prospectus, advertisements, notices of deficiency. LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- Reading a result (the rule of 2026-10-29): JUST TRUE is yes; JUST FALSE is "the TEXT says no in its own words"; NOTHING is "the text does not say".
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. Every "no" branch carries `-- FALSE-kind (...)`, every "not covered" branch `-- NOTHING-kind (...)`.
-- A consent bar, a bar on advertising and a bar on dissemination are answered JUST TRUE where the act is a contravention; an offence function takes that answer as an input.
-- Answers of other functions are passed in as MAYBE BOOLEAN inputs; for an exemption or a route that opens a door only JUST TRUE counts (fork F40).
-- "Before" and "After" a registration are read as windows the text fixes in its own words; outside it a route answers JUST FALSE (fork F39, split site (ii)).
-- Deadlines: "within N days after" counts an act on the event's day as in time (fork F9); the period of s 250(3) uses the keel's months (fork F36).

-- inert (reason 1), lines 40240-40241: s 249 marginal heading: not operative.
-- inert (reason 1), lines 40307-40308: s 249A marginal heading: not operative.
-- inert (reason 1), lines 40375-40375: s 250 marginal heading: not operative.
-- inert (reason 1), lines 40440-40440: s 251 marginal heading: not operative.
-- repealed or blank in this text, lines 40517-40517: s 251(3)(a)(ii): "[Deleted by Act 12 of 2026 wef 29/06/2026]".
-- inert (reason 1), lines 40923-40924: s 252 marginal heading: not operative.

DECLARE `s 249 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 249(1) issue the prospectus or profile statement without the expert's consent`
    `s 249A(1) issue the prospectus or profile statement without the issue manager's consent`
    `s 249A(2) issue the prospectus or profile statement without the underwriter's consent`
    `s 249(4) contravene the condition or restriction`

DECLARE `s 250 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 250(1) make the offer or allot, issue or sell on the basis of an expired prospectus`
    `s 250(2) authorise or permit the offer, or the allotment, issue or sale, on the basis of an expired prospectus`

DECLARE `s 251 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 251(1) advertise the offer or intended offer or publish the statement`
    `s 251(15) contravene the condition or restriction`

§ `s 249: the expert's consent`

-- src:40243 | 249.—(1) Where an offer of securities or securities‑based
-- src:40244 | derivatives contracts is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or
-- src:40249 | profile statement which includes a statement purporting to be made
-- src:40250 | by, or based on a statement made by, an expert, the prospectus or
-- src:40251 | profile statement must not be issued unless —
-- src:40253 | (a) the expert has given, and has not before the registration of
-- src:40254 | the prospectus or profile statement (as the case may be)
-- src:40255 | withdrawn his or her written consent to the issue thereof
-- src:40256 | with the statement included in the form and context in
-- src:40257 | which it is included; and
-- src:40259 | (b) there appears in the prospectus or profile statement (as the
-- src:40260 | case may be) a statement that the expert has given and has
-- src:40261 | not withdrawn his or her consent.
@ref s 249(1) (src:40243-40261)
GIVEN
    `an offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts made in, or accompanied by, a prospectus or profile statement?
    `the prospectus or profile statement includes a statement purporting to be made by, or based on a statement made by, an expert` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus or profile statement include a statement purporting to be made by, or based on a statement made by, an expert?
    `the person or the prospectus or profile statement is exempt under subsection (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 249(3) the person or document is exempt from the section` answer for the person or the prospectus or profile statement? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the expert has given written consent and has not withdrawn it before the registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the expert given written consent (and not withdrawn it before the registration of the prospectus or profile statement) to the issue of the prospectus or profile statement with the statement included in the form and context in which it is included?
    `there appears in the prospectus or profile statement a statement that the expert has given and has not withdrawn the consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus or profile statement contain a statement that the expert has given, and has not withdrawn, the consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 249(1) the prospectus or profile statement must not be issued` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`an offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement` AND `the prospectus or profile statement includes a statement purporting to be made by, or based on a statement made by, an expert`))
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement which includes a statement purporting to be made by, or based on a statement made by, an expert, the prospectus or profile statement must not be issued unless"
        IF (`the person or the prospectus or profile statement is exempt under subsection (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Authority may exempt any person or class of persons, or any prospectus or profile statement or class or description of prospectuses or profile statements, from this section"
        IF `the expert has given written consent and has not withdrawn it before the registration` AND `there appears in the prospectus or profile statement a statement that the expert has given and has not withdrawn the consent`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be issued unless (a) the expert has given, and has not before the registration of the prospectus or profile statement (as the case may be) withdrawn his or her written consent to the issue thereof with the statement included in the form and context in which it is included; and (b) there appears in the prospectus or profile statement (as the case may be) a statement that the expert has given and has not withdrawn his or her consent"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 249(1) (the prohibition as a rule) (src:40243-40261)
GIVEN
    `the person` IS A Party @desc Who issues the prospectus or profile statement?
    `what section 249(1) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 249(1) the prospectus or profile statement must not be issued` answer for the prospectus or profile statement? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 249 action`
`s 249(1) the person shall not issue the prospectus or profile statement` MEANS
    IF `what section 249(1) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `s 249(1) issue the prospectus or profile statement without the expert's consent`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "the prospectus or profile statement was issued without the expert's written consent, or without the statement that the consent was given; section 249(2) makes that an offence"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:40265 | (1A) Every person making the offer must cause a true copy of every
-- src:40266 | written consent referred to in subsection (1) to be deposited, within
-- src:40267 | 7 days after the registration of the prospectus or profile statement, at
-- src:40268 | the registered office of the issuer in Singapore or, if the issuer has no
-- src:40269 | registered office in Singapore, at the address in Singapore specified in
-- src:40270 | the prospectus for that purpose.
@ref s 249(1A) (src:40265-40270)
GIVEN
    `a written consent referred to in subsection (1) has been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a written consent referred to in subsection (1) been given?
    `the date of the registration of the prospectus or profile statement` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the prospectus or profile statement registered?
    `the issuer has a registered office in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the issuer have a registered office in Singapore?
    `a true copy of every written consent has been deposited at the registered office of the issuer in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you deposited a true copy of every written consent at the registered office of the issuer in Singapore?
    `a true copy of every written consent has been deposited at the address in Singapore specified in the prospectus for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you deposited a true copy of every written consent at the address in Singapore specified in the prospectus for that purpose?
    `the date the copies were deposited` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you deposit the copies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 249(1A) the person making the offer has deposited the copies of the consents` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a written consent referred to in subsection (1) has been given`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every written consent referred to in subsection (1)"
        IF (IF `the issuer has a registered office in Singapore` THEN `a true copy of every written consent has been deposited at the registered office of the issuer in Singapore` ELSE `a true copy of every written consent has been deposited at the address in Singapore specified in the prospectus for that purpose`) AND (`the date the copies were deposited` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the registration of the prospectus or profile statement` 7 Days))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must cause a true copy of every written consent referred to in subsection (1) to be deposited, within 7 days after the registration of the prospectus or profile statement, at the registered office of the issuer in Singapore or, if"

-- src:40272 | (1B) Every issuer must keep, and make available for inspection by
-- src:40273 | its members and creditors and persons who have subscribed for or
-- src:40274 | purchased the securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts to
-- src:40275 | which the prospectus or profile statement relates, without payment of
-- src:40276 | any fee, a true copy of every written consent deposited in accordance
-- src:40277 | with subsection (1A) for a period of at least 6 months after the
-- src:40278 | registration of the prospectus or profile statement.
@ref s 249(1B) (src:40272-40278)
GIVEN
    `a written consent has been deposited in accordance with subsection (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a written consent been deposited in accordance with subsection (1A)?
    `the date of the registration of the prospectus or profile statement` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the prospectus or profile statement registered?
    `the issuer keeps a true copy of every written consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the issuer keep a true copy of every written consent deposited?
    `the issuer makes it available for inspection without payment of any fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the issuer make it available for inspection by its members and creditors and persons who have subscribed for or purchased the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, without payment of any fee?
    `the date until which the issuer keeps the copy` IS A DATE @desc Until what date does the issuer keep the copy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 249(1B) the issuer has kept the copies and made them available` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a written consent has been deposited in accordance with subsection (1A)`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every written consent deposited in accordance with subsection (1A)"
        IF `the issuer keeps a true copy of every written consent` AND `the issuer makes it available for inspection without payment of any fee` AND (`the date until which the issuer keeps the copy` AT LEAST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the registration of the prospectus or profile statement` 6 Months))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must keep, and make available for inspection by its members and creditors and persons who have subscribed for or purchased the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts to which the prospectus or profile statement relates, without payment of any fee, a true copy of every written consent deposited in accordance with subsection (1A) for a period of at least 6 months after the registration of the prospectus or profile statement"

-- src:40282 | (2) If any prospectus or profile statement is issued in contravention
-- src:40283 | of subsection (1), the person making the offer and every person who
-- src:40284 | is knowingly a party to the issue thereof shall be guilty of an offence
-- src:40285 | and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000 or to
-- src:40286 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both and, in
-- src:40287 | the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding
-- src:40288 | $5,000 for every day or part of a day during which the offence
-- src:40289 | continues after conviction.
@ref s 249(2) (src:40282-40289)
GIVEN
    `what section 249(1) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 249(1) the prospectus or profile statement must not be issued` answer for the prospectus or profile statement? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the prospectus or profile statement is issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the prospectus or profile statement issued?
    `the person is the person making the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the person making the offer?
    `the person is knowingly a party to the issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you knowingly a party to the issue of the prospectus or profile statement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F33 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 249(2) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the prospectus or profile statement is issued`) OR ((`what section 249(1) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE))
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any prospectus or profile statement is issued in contravention of subsection (1)"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)  -- MARGINAL-READING (a)
        IF (NOT ((`what section 249(1) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE)))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an answer under subsection (1) was not worked out
        IF `the person is the person making the offer` OR `the person is knowingly a party to the issue`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the person making the offer and every person who is knowingly a party to the issue thereof shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)

@ref s 249(2) (the penalty) (src:40282-40289)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 249(2) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 50000, 12, TRUE, 5000  -- a fine not exceeding $50,000, or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months, or both; a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

-- src:40291 | (3) The Authority may exempt any person or class of persons, or
-- src:40292 | any prospectus or profile statement or class or description of
-- src:40297 | prospectuses or profile statements, from this section, subject to such
-- src:40298 | conditions or restrictions as the Authority may determine.
@ref s 249(3) (src:40291-40298)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has exempted the person, the document, or a class to which it belongs, from the section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority exempted you, or the prospectus or profile statement, or a class to which it belongs, from this section?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 249(3) the person or document is exempt from the section` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has exempted the person, the document, or a class to which it belongs, from the section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Authority may exempt any person or class of persons, or any prospectus or profile statement or class or description of prospectuses or profile statements, from this section"

-- src:40300 | (4) Any person who contravenes any of the conditions or
-- src:40301 | restrictions imposed under subsection (3) shall be guilty of an
-- src:40302 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:40303 | $50,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:40304 | exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day during which the
-- src:40305 | offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 249(4) (src:40300-40305)
GIVEN
    `the person contravenes a condition or restriction imposed under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you contravene a condition or restriction imposed under subsection (3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F34 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 249(4) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes a condition or restriction imposed under subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who contravenes any of the conditions or restrictions imposed under subsection (3) shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)

@ref s 249(4) (the penalty) (src:40300-40305)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 249(4) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 50000, 0, FALSE, 5000  -- a fine not exceeding $50,000; no imprisonment is stated (0); a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

@ref s 249(4) (the prohibition as a rule) (src:40300-40305)
GIVEN
    `the person` IS A Party @desc Who is bound by the condition or restriction?
    `the person is exempt under subsection (3) subject to a condition or restriction in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person (or the prospectus or profile statement) exempt under section 249(3) subject to a condition or restriction that is in force?
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 249 action`
`s 249(4) the person shall not contravene a condition or restriction` MEANS
    IF `the person is exempt under subsection (3) subject to a condition or restriction in force`
    THEN PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `s 249(4) contravene the condition or restriction`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "a condition or restriction imposed under section 249(3) was contravened, which is an offence under section 249(4)"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `s 249A: the consent of an issue manager or an underwriter`

-- src:40310 | 249A.—(1) Where an offer of securities or securities‑based
-- src:40311 | derivatives contracts is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or
-- src:40312 | profile statement in which a person is named as the issue manager to
-- src:40313 | the offer, the prospectus or profile statement must not be issued
-- src:40314 | unless —
-- src:40316 | (a) the person has given, and has not before the registration of
-- src:40317 | the prospectus or profile statement (as the case may be)
-- src:40318 | withdrawn the person’s written consent to being named in
-- src:40319 | the prospectus or profile statement as issue manager to that
-- src:40320 | offer; and
-- src:40322 | (b) there appears in the prospectus or profile statement (as the
-- src:40323 | case may be) a statement that the person has given and has
-- src:40324 | not withdrawn the person’s consent.
@ref s 249A(1) (src:40310-40324)
GIVEN
    `an offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts made in, or accompanied by, a prospectus or profile statement?
    `the prospectus or profile statement names a person as the issue manager to the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus or profile statement name a person as the issue manager to the offer?
    `the issue manager has given written consent and has not withdrawn it before the registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the issue manager given written consent (and not withdrawn it before the registration of the prospectus or profile statement) to being named in the prospectus or profile statement as issue manager to that offer?
    `there appears in the prospectus or profile statement a statement that the issue manager has given and has not withdrawn the consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus or profile statement contain a statement that the issue manager has given, and has not withdrawn, the consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 249A(1) the prospectus or profile statement must not be issued` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`an offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement` AND `the prospectus or profile statement names a person as the issue manager to the offer`))
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement in which a person is named as the issue manager to the offer, the prospectus or profile statement must not be issued unless"
        IF `the issue manager has given written consent and has not withdrawn it before the registration` AND `there appears in the prospectus or profile statement a statement that the issue manager has given and has not withdrawn the consent`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be issued unless (a) the person has given, and has not before the registration of the prospectus or profile statement (as the case may be) withdrawn the person's written consent to being named in the prospectus or profile statement as issue manager to that offer; and (b) there appears in the prospectus or profile statement (as the case may be) a statement that the person has given and has not withdrawn the person's consent"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 249A(1) (the prohibition as a rule) (src:40310-40324)
GIVEN
    `the person` IS A Party @desc Who issues the prospectus or profile statement?
    `what section 249A(1) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 249A(1) the prospectus or profile statement must not be issued` answer for the prospectus or profile statement? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 249 action`
`s 249A(1) the person shall not issue the prospectus or profile statement` MEANS
    IF `what section 249A(1) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `s 249A(1) issue the prospectus or profile statement without the issue manager's consent`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "the prospectus or profile statement was issued without the issue manager's written consent, or without the statement that the consent was given; section 249A(3) makes that an offence"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:40328 | (2) Where an offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:40329 | contracts is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile
-- src:40330 | statement in which a person is named as the underwriter (but not a
-- src:40331 | sub‑underwriter) to the offer, the prospectus or profile statement must
-- src:40332 | not be issued unless —
-- src:40334 | (a) the person has given, and has not before the registration of
-- src:40335 | the prospectus or profile statement (as the case may be)
-- src:40336 | withdrawn the person’s written consent to being named in
-- src:40337 | the prospectus or profile statement as underwriter to that
-- src:40338 | offer; and
-- src:40343 | (b) there appears in the prospectus or profile statement (as the
-- src:40344 | case may be) a statement that the person has given and has
-- src:40345 | not withdrawn such consent.
@ref s 249A(2) (src:40328-40345)
GIVEN
    `an offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts made in, or accompanied by, a prospectus or profile statement?
    `the prospectus or profile statement names a person as the underwriter (but not a sub-underwriter) to the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus or profile statement name a person as the underwriter (but not a sub-underwriter) to the offer?
    `the underwriter has given written consent and has not withdrawn it before the registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the underwriter given written consent (and not withdrawn it before the registration of the prospectus or profile statement) to being named in the prospectus or profile statement as underwriter to that offer?
    `there appears in the prospectus or profile statement a statement that the underwriter has given and has not withdrawn the consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus or profile statement contain a statement that the underwriter has given, and has not withdrawn, the consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 249A(2) the prospectus or profile statement must not be issued` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`an offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement` AND `the prospectus or profile statement names a person as the underwriter (but not a sub-underwriter) to the offer`))
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement in which a person is named as the underwriter (but not a sub-underwriter) to the offer, the prospectus or profile statement must not be issued unless"
        IF `the underwriter has given written consent and has not withdrawn it before the registration` AND `there appears in the prospectus or profile statement a statement that the underwriter has given and has not withdrawn the consent`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be issued unless (a) the person has given, and has not before the registration of the prospectus or profile statement (as the case may be) withdrawn the person's written consent to being named in the prospectus or profile statement as underwriter to that offer; and (b) there appears in the prospectus or profile statement (as the case may be) a statement that the person has given and has not withdrawn such consent"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 249A(2) (the prohibition as a rule) (src:40328-40345)
GIVEN
    `the person` IS A Party @desc Who issues the prospectus or profile statement?
    `what section 249A(2) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 249A(2) the prospectus or profile statement must not be issued` answer for the prospectus or profile statement? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 249 action`
`s 249A(2) the person shall not issue the prospectus or profile statement` MEANS
    IF `what section 249A(2) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `s 249A(2) issue the prospectus or profile statement without the underwriter's consent`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "the prospectus or profile statement was issued without the underwriter's written consent, or without the statement that the consent was given; section 249A(3) makes that an offence"
    ELSE FULFILLED

