GIVEN
    `what section 249A(1) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 249A(1) the prospectus or profile statement must not be issued` answer for the prospectus or profile statement? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 249A(2) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 249A(2) the prospectus or profile statement must not be issued` answer for the prospectus or profile statement? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the prospectus or profile statement is issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the prospectus or profile statement issued?
    `the person is the person making the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the person making the offer?
    `the person is knowingly a party to the issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you knowingly a party to the issue of the prospectus or profile statement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F35 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 249A(3) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the prospectus or profile statement is issued`) OR ((`what section 249A(1) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`what section 249A(2) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE))
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any prospectus or profile statement is issued in contravention of subsection (1) or (2)"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)  -- MARGINAL-READING (a)
        IF (NOT ((`what section 249A(1) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 249A(2) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE)))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an answer under subsection (1) or (2) was not worked out
        IF `the person is the person making the offer` OR `the person is knowingly a party to the issue`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the person making the offer and every person who is knowingly a party to the issue thereof shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)

@ref s 249A(3) (the penalty) (src:40349-40356)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 249A(3) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 50000, 12, TRUE, 5000  -- a fine not exceeding $50,000, or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months, or both; a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

-- src:40358 | (4) Every person making the offer must cause a true copy of every
-- src:40359 | written consent referred to in subsections (1) and (2) to be deposited,
-- src:40360 | within 7 days after the registration of the prospectus or profile
-- src:40361 | statement, at the registered office of the issuer in Singapore or, if it
-- src:40362 | has no registered office in Singapore, at the address in Singapore
-- src:40363 | specified in the prospectus for that purpose.
@ref s 249A(4) (src:40358-40363)
GIVEN
    `a written consent referred to in subsections (1) and (2) has been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a written consent referred to in subsections (1) and (2) been given?
    `the date of the registration of the prospectus or profile statement` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the prospectus or profile statement registered?
    `the issuer has a registered office in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the issuer have a registered office in Singapore?
    `a true copy of every written consent has been deposited at the registered office of the issuer in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you deposited a true copy of every written consent at the registered office of the issuer in Singapore?
    `a true copy of every written consent has been deposited at the address in Singapore specified in the prospectus for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you deposited a true copy of every written consent at the address in Singapore specified in the prospectus for that purpose?
    `the date the copies were deposited` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you deposit the copies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 249A(4) the person making the offer has deposited the copies of the consents` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a written consent referred to in subsections (1) and (2) has been given`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every written consent referred to in subsections (1) and (2)"
        IF (IF `the issuer has a registered office in Singapore` THEN `a true copy of every written consent has been deposited at the registered office of the issuer in Singapore` ELSE `a true copy of every written consent has been deposited at the address in Singapore specified in the prospectus for that purpose`) AND (`the date the copies were deposited` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the registration of the prospectus or profile statement` 7 Days))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must cause a true copy of every written consent referred to in subsections (1) and (2) to be deposited, within 7 days after the registration of the prospectus or profile statement, at the registered office of the issuer in Singapore or, if"

-- src:40365 | (5) Every issuer must keep, and make available for inspection by its
-- src:40366 | members and creditors and persons who have subscribed for or
-- src:40367 | purchased the securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts to
-- src:40368 | which the prospectus or profile statement relates, without payment of
-- src:40369 | any fee, a true copy of every written consent deposited in accordance
-- src:40370 | with subsection (4) for a period of at least 6 months after the
-- src:40371 | registration of the prospectus or profile statement.
@ref s 249A(5) (src:40365-40371)
GIVEN
    `a written consent has been deposited in accordance with subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a written consent been deposited in accordance with subsection (4)?
    `the date of the registration of the prospectus or profile statement` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the prospectus or profile statement registered?
    `the issuer keeps a true copy of every written consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the issuer keep a true copy of every written consent deposited?
    `the issuer makes it available for inspection without payment of any fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the issuer make it available for inspection by its members and creditors and persons who have subscribed for or purchased the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, without payment of any fee?
    `the date until which the issuer keeps the copy` IS A DATE @desc Until what date does the issuer keep the copy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 249A(5) the issuer has kept the copies and made them available` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a written consent has been deposited in accordance with subsection (4)`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every written consent deposited in accordance with subsection (4)"
        IF `the issuer keeps a true copy of every written consent` AND `the issuer makes it available for inspection without payment of any fee` AND (`the date until which the issuer keeps the copy` AT LEAST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the registration of the prospectus or profile statement` 6 Months))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must keep, and make available for inspection by its members and creditors and persons who have subscribed for or purchased the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts to which the prospectus or profile statement relates, without payment of any fee, a true copy of every written consent deposited in accordance with subsection (4) for a period of at least 6 months after the registration of the prospectus or profile statement"
§ `s 250: how long a prospectus or profile statement is valid`

-- s 250(3): the period. 24 months from the registration of the base prospectus for a debenture issuance programme; 6 months from the registration in any other case.
-- src:40407 | (3) The period under subsection (1) or (2) is —
-- src:40409 | (a) in a case where the securities or securities‑based
-- src:40410 | derivatives contracts are debentures or units of
-- src:40411 | debentures issued under a debenture issuance programme
-- src:40412 | under section 240A, 24 months from the date of
-- src:40413 | registration by the Authority of the base prospectus in
-- src:40414 | relation to such offer, allotment, issue or sale; or
-- src:40416 | (b) in any other case, 6 months from the date of registration by
-- src:40417 | the Authority of the prospectus in relation to such offer,
-- src:40418 | allotment, issue or sale.
@ref s 250(3) (src:40407-40418)
GIVEN
    `the securities or contracts are debentures or units of debentures issued under a debenture issuance programme under section 240A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities debentures or units of debentures issued under a debenture issuance programme under section 240A?
    `the date of registration by the Authority of the base prospectus or prospectus` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Authority register the base prospectus (for a debenture issuance programme) or the prospectus?
GIVETH A DATE
`s 250(3) the last day of the period` MEANS
    IF `the securities or contracts are debentures or units of debentures issued under a debenture issuance programme under section 240A`
    THEN `period: the last day of a period after` `the date of registration by the Authority of the base prospectus or prospectus` 24 Months
    ELSE `period: the last day of a period after` `the date of registration by the Authority of the base prospectus or prospectus` 6 Months

-- s 250(1): the bar on offering, allotting, issuing or selling on a prospectus after the period.
-- src:40377 | 250.—(1) A person must not make an offer of securities or
-- src:40378 | securities‑based derivatives contracts, or allot, issue or sell any
-- src:40379 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts, on the basis of a
-- src:40380 | prospectus or profile statement after the expiration of the period
-- src:40381 | referred to in subsection (3).
@ref s 250(1) (src:40377-40381)
GIVEN
    `the person makes an offer, or allots, issues or sells securities or contracts, on the basis of a prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make an offer, or allot, issue or sell securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, on the basis of a prospectus or profile statement?
    `the day of the offer, allotment, issue or sale` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make the offer, or allot, issue or sell?
    `the last day of the period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period in section 250(3) (what does the function `s 250(3) the last day of the period` answer)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F36 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 250(1) the person must not make the offer or allot, issue or sell on the basis of the prospectus` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person makes an offer, or allots, issues or sells securities or contracts, on the basis of a prospectus or profile statement`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person must not make an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, or allot, issue or sell any securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, on the basis of a prospectus or profile statement"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        IF `the day of the offer, allotment, issue or sale` AT MOST `the last day of the period`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after the expiration of the period referred to in subsection (3)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 250(1) (the prohibition as a rule) (src:40377-40381)
GIVEN
    `the person` IS A Party @desc Who makes the offer, or allots, issues or sells?
    `what section 250(1) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 250(1) the person must not make the offer or allot, issue or sell on the basis of the prospectus` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 250 action`
`s 250(1) the person shall not make the offer or allot, issue or sell after the period` MEANS
    IF `what section 250(1) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `s 250(1) make the offer or allot, issue or sell on the basis of an expired prospectus`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "an offer was made, or securities were allotted, issued or sold, on the basis of a prospectus or profile statement after the period in section 250(3); section 250(4) makes that an offence"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 250(2): an officer, equivalent person or promoter must not authorise or permit it. "In a case where" is a "where" gate (rule (b)).
-- src:40385 | (2) In a case where an entity makes an offer of securities or
-- src:40386 | securities‑based derivatives contracts or where the securities or
-- src:40387 | securities‑based derivatives contracts being offered are those issued
-- src:40392 | by an entity or a proposed entity, an officer or equivalent person or a
-- src:40393 | promoter of the entity or proposed entity must not authorise or
-- src:40394 | permit —
-- src:40396 | (a) the offer of those securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:40397 | contracts; or
-- src:40399 | (b) the allotment, issue or sale of those securities or
-- src:40400 | securities‑based derivatives contracts,
-- src:40402 | on the basis of a prospectus or profile statement after the expiration of
-- src:40403 | the period referred to in subsection (3).
@ref s 250(2) (src:40385-40403)
GIVEN
    `an entity makes the offer, or the securities or contracts are issued by an entity or a proposed entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an entity make the offer, or are the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts offered issued by an entity or a proposed entity?
    `the person is an officer or equivalent person or a promoter of the entity or proposed entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or equivalent person, or a promoter, of the entity or proposed entity?
    `the person authorises or permits the offer, or the allotment, issue or sale, on the basis of a prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you authorise or permit the offer, or the allotment, issue or sale, of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts on the basis of a prospectus or profile statement?
    `the day of the offer, allotment, issue or sale` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the offer made, or the allotment, issue or sale done?
    `the last day of the period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period in section 250(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F36 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 250(2) the officer or promoter must not authorise or permit the offer, allotment, issue or sale` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `an entity makes the offer, or the securities or contracts are issued by an entity or a proposed entity`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In a case where an entity makes an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts or where the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts being offered are those issued by an entity or a proposed entity"
        IF (NOT `the person is an officer or equivalent person or a promoter of the entity or proposed entity`) OR (NOT `the person authorises or permits the offer, or the allotment, issue or sale, on the basis of a prospectus or profile statement`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an officer or equivalent person or a promoter of the entity or proposed entity must not authorise or permit"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        IF `the day of the offer, allotment, issue or sale` AT MOST `the last day of the period`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on the basis of a prospectus or profile statement after the expiration of the period referred to in subsection (3)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 250(2) (the prohibition as a rule) (src:40385-40403)
GIVEN
    `the person` IS A Party @desc Who is the officer or equivalent person or promoter?
    `what section 250(2) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 250(2) the officer or promoter must not authorise or permit the offer, allotment, issue or sale` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 250 action`
`s 250(2) the officer or promoter shall not authorise or permit the offer, allotment, issue or sale after the period` MEANS
    IF `what section 250(2) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `s 250(2) authorise or permit the offer, or the allotment, issue or sale, on the basis of an expired prospectus`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "the offer, allotment, issue or sale was authorised or permitted on the basis of a prospectus or profile statement after the period in section 250(3); section 250(4) makes that an offence"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 250(4): the offence of default in complying with (1) or (2), and its penalty. "If default is made" opens it: a failed "if" is the text's no (reading (a), as at s 240(17)).
-- src:40422 | (4) If default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (2), the
-- src:40423 | person and, in the case of an entity or a proposed entity, every officer
-- src:40424 | or equivalent person or promoter of the entity or proposed entity shall
-- src:40425 | be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:40426 | exceeding $50,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:40427 | 12 months or to both and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a
-- src:40428 | further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day during
-- src:40429 | which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 250(4) (src:40422-40429)
GIVEN
    `what section 250(1) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 250(1) the person must not make the offer or allot, issue or sell on the basis of the prospectus` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 250(2) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 250(2) the officer or promoter must not authorise or permit the offer, allotment, issue or sale` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the person is an officer or equivalent person or a promoter of an entity or proposed entity in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or equivalent person, or a promoter, of an entity or proposed entity that is in default under section 250(1) or (2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F37 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 250(4) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`what section 250(1) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 250(2) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the person is an officer or equivalent person or a promoter of an entity or proposed entity in default`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`what section 250(1) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`what section 250(2) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (1) or (2)"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)  -- MARGINAL-READING (a)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an answer under subsection (1) or (2) was not worked out

@ref s 250(4) (the penalty) (src:40422-40429)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 250(4) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 50000, 12, TRUE, 5000  -- a fine not exceeding $50,000, or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months, or both; a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

-- s 250(5): an allotment, issue or sale made in contravention is not, by reason only of that fact, voidable or void. A flat negative.
-- src:40431 | (5) An allotment, an issue or a sale of securities or securities‑based
-- src:40432 | derivatives contracts that is made in contravention of subsection (1)
-- src:40433 | or (2) is not, by reason only of that fact, voidable or void.
@ref s 250(5) (src:40431-40433)
GIVEN
    `the allotment, issue or sale is made in contravention of subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the allotment, issue or sale made in contravention of section 250(1) or (2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 250(5) the allotment, issue or sale is void or voidable by reason only of the contravention` MEANS
    IF `the allotment, issue or sale is made in contravention of subsection (1) or (2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not, by reason only of that fact, voidable or void"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative names an allotment, issue or sale made in contravention and says nothing of any other

§ `s 251: restrictions on advertisements`

-- s 251(1): the bar on advertising and publishing. "If a prospectus is required" is a failed "if" (reading (a)); the three acts are the elements the bar is limited to; "unless ... authorised by this section" is a closed gate (only an authorisation answered JUST TRUE counts).
-- src:40442 | 251.—(1) If a prospectus is required for an offer or intended offer
-- src:40443 | of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts, a person must
-- src:40444 | not —
-- src:40446 | (a) advertise the offer or intended offer; or
-- src:40448 | (b) publish a statement that —
-- src:40450 | (i) directly or indirectly refers to the offer or intended
-- src:40451 | offer; or
-- src:40453 | (ii) is reasonably likely to induce persons to subscribe
-- src:40454 | for or purchase the securities or securities‑based
-- src:40455 | derivatives contracts,
-- src:40457 | unless the advertisement or publication is authorised by this section.
@ref s 251(1) (src:40442-40457)
GIVEN
    `a prospectus is required for the offer or intended offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a prospectus required for the offer or intended offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the person advertises the offer or intended offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you advertise the offer or intended offer?
    `the person publishes a statement that directly or indirectly refers to the offer or intended offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you publish a statement that directly or indirectly refers to the offer or intended offer?
    `the person publishes a statement that is reasonably likely to induce persons to subscribe for or purchase the securities or contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you publish a statement that is reasonably likely to induce persons to subscribe for or purchase the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the advertisement or publication is authorised by this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251 the advertisement or publication is authorised by this section` answer for the advertisement or publication? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the person is exempt under subsection (14)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(14) the person is exempt from this section` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F38 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(1) the person must not advertise the offer or publish the statement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a prospectus is required for the offer or intended offer`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a prospectus is required for an offer or intended offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, a person must not"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)  -- MARGINAL-READING (a)
        IF (NOT (`the person advertises the offer or intended offer` OR `the person publishes a statement that directly or indirectly refers to the offer or intended offer` OR `the person publishes a statement that is reasonably likely to induce persons to subscribe for or purchase the securities or contracts`))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person must not ... advertise the offer or intended offer ... publish a statement that"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        IF (`the advertisement or publication is authorised by this section` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is exempt under subsection (14)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the advertisement or publication is authorised by this section"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 251(1) (the prohibition as a rule) (src:40442-40457)
GIVEN
    `the person` IS A Party @desc Who advertises the offer or publishes the statement?
    `what section 251(1) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(1) the person must not advertise the offer or publish the statement` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 251 action`
`s 251(1) the person shall not advertise the offer or publish the statement` MEANS
    IF `what section 251(1) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `s 251(1) advertise the offer or intended offer or publish the statement`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "the offer was advertised, or the statement published, although a prospectus was required and the act was not authorised by section 251; section 251(12) makes that an offence"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 251(2): in determining whether a statement indirectly refers to an offer, or is reasonably likely to induce, "regard must be had to" three matters. A duty on whoever determines; the text does not say how the matters weigh, so it gives no verdict on the statement (fork F41).
-- src:40461 | (2) In determining whether a statement —
-- src:40463 | (a) indirectly refers to an offer or intended offer of securities or
-- src:40464 | securities‑based derivatives contracts; or
-- src:40466 | (b) is reasonably likely to induce persons to subscribe for or
-- src:40467 | purchase securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:40468 | contracts,
-- src:40470 | regard must be had to whether the statement —
-- src:40472 | (c) forms part of the normal advertising —
-- src:40474 | (i) of an entity’s products or services and is genuinely
-- src:40475 | directed at maintaining its existing customers, or
-- src:40476 | attracting new customers, for those products or
-- src:40477 | services; or
-- src:40479 | (ii) by a trustee‑manager of a business trust on behalf of
-- src:40480 | the business trust in respect of the products or
-- src:40481 | services offered by the trustee‑manager on behalf of
-- src:40482 | the business trust, and is genuinely directed at
-- src:40483 | maintaining existing customers, or attracting new
-- src:40484 | customers, for those products or services;
-- src:40486 | (d) communicates information that materially deals with the
-- src:40487 | affairs of the entity or the business trust; and
-- src:40492 | (e) is likely to encourage investment decisions being made on
-- src:40493 | the basis of the statement rather than on the basis of
-- src:40494 | information contained in a prospectus or profile statement.
@ref s 251(2) (src:40461-40494)
GIVEN
    `a determination is made whether a statement indirectly refers to an offer or intended offer or is reasonably likely to induce persons to subscribe for or purchase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it being determined whether a statement indirectly refers to an offer or intended offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, or is reasonably likely to induce persons to subscribe for or purchase them?
    `regard is had to whether the statement forms part of the normal advertising described in paragraph (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is regard had to whether the statement forms part of the normal advertising described in section 251(2)(c)?
    `regard is had to whether the statement communicates information that materially deals with the affairs of the entity or the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is regard had to whether the statement communicates information that materially deals with the affairs of the entity or the business trust?
    `regard is had to whether the statement is likely to encourage investment decisions being made on the basis of the statement rather than on the basis of information in a prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is regard had to whether the statement is likely to encourage investment decisions being made on the basis of the statement rather than on the basis of information contained in a prospectus or profile statement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F41 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(2) regard has been had to the three matters` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a determination is made whether a statement indirectly refers to an offer or intended offer or is reasonably likely to induce persons to subscribe for or purchase`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In determining whether a statement"
        IF `regard is had to whether the statement forms part of the normal advertising described in paragraph (c)` AND `regard is had to whether the statement communicates information that materially deals with the affairs of the entity or the business trust` AND `regard is had to whether the statement is likely to encourage investment decisions being made on the basis of the statement rather than on the basis of information in a prospectus or profile statement`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "regard must be had to whether the statement"

-- s 251(2)(c): the first of the three matters, the normal advertising. Two limbs, (i) an entity's own products or services, (ii) a trustee-manager's on behalf of a business trust; each needs the genuine direction at customers. The list of limbs is not closed.
-- src:40472 | (c) forms part of the normal advertising —
-- src:40474 | (i) of an entity’s products or services and is genuinely
-- src:40475 | directed at maintaining its existing customers, or
-- src:40476 | attracting new customers, for those products or
-- src:40477 | services; or
-- src:40479 | (ii) by a trustee‑manager of a business trust on behalf of
-- src:40480 | the business trust in respect of the products or
-- src:40481 | services offered by the trustee‑manager on behalf of
-- src:40482 | the business trust, and is genuinely directed at
-- src:40483 | maintaining existing customers, or attracting new
-- src:40484 | customers, for those products or services;
@ref s 251(2)(c) (src:40472-40484)
GIVEN
    `the statement forms part of the normal advertising of an entity's products or services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement form part of the normal advertising of an entity's products or services?
    `it is genuinely directed at maintaining the entity's existing customers or attracting new customers for those products or services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement genuinely directed at maintaining the entity's existing customers, or attracting new customers, for those products or services?
    `the statement forms part of the normal advertising by a trustee-manager of a business trust on behalf of the business trust in respect of the products or services it offers on behalf of the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement form part of the normal advertising by a trustee-manager of a business trust, on behalf of the business trust, in respect of the products or services offered by the trustee-manager on behalf of the business trust?
    `it is genuinely directed at maintaining the business trust's existing customers or attracting new customers for those products or services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement genuinely directed at maintaining existing customers, or attracting new customers, for those products or services of the business trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 251(2)(c) the statement forms part of the normal advertising` MEANS
    IF (`the statement forms part of the normal advertising of an entity's products or services` AND `it is genuinely directed at maintaining the entity's existing customers or attracting new customers for those products or services`) OR (`the statement forms part of the normal advertising by a trustee-manager of a business trust on behalf of the business trust in respect of the products or services it offers on behalf of the business trust` AND `it is genuinely directed at maintaining the business trust's existing customers or attracting new customers for those products or services`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text says what the matter is by two limbs and does not say that a statement outside both is not normal advertising

-- s 251(3): the preliminary document. "Despite subsection (6)" only lifts the "contains only" limit of subsection (6) from this route: the two routes are separate functions and the combiner takes either. Gated by "before ... is registered" (a window, split site (ii), fork F39) and by the document being one lodged with the Authority (a scope limit, NOTHING).
-- src:40498 | (3) Despite subsection (6), a person may, before a prospectus or
-- src:40499 | profile statement is registered by the Authority, disseminate a
-- src:40500 | preliminary document which has been lodged with the Authority to
-- src:40501 | any person without contravening subsection (1), if —
-- src:40503 | (a) the front page of the preliminary document contains —
-- src:40505 | (i) the following statement:
-- src:40507 | . “This is a preliminary document and is subject to
-- src:40509 | further amendments and completion in the
-- src:40511 | prospectus to be registered by the Monetary
-- src:40513 | Authority of Singapore.”; and
-- src:40517 | (ii) [Deleted by Act 12 of 2026 wef 29/06/2026]
-- src:40519 | (iii) a statement in bold lettering that no offer or
-- src:40520 | agreement may be made on the basis of the
-- src:40521 | preliminary document to purchase or subscribe for
-- src:40522 | any securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:40523 | contracts to which the preliminary document relates;
-- src:40525 | (b) the preliminary document does not contain or have
-- src:40526 | attached to it any form of application that will facilitate
-- src:40527 | the making by any person of an offer of the securities or
-- src:40528 | securities‑based derivatives contracts to which the
-- src:40529 | preliminary document relates, or the acceptance of such
-- src:40530 | an offer by any person; and
-- src:40532 | (c) when the prospectus is registered by the Authority, the
-- src:40533 | person takes reasonable steps to notify the persons to
-- src:40534 | whom the preliminary document was issued that the
-- src:40535 | registered prospectus is available for collection.
@ref s 251(3) (src:40498-40535)
GIVEN
    `the person disseminates a preliminary document to any person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you disseminate a preliminary document to any person?
    `the preliminary document has been lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the preliminary document been lodged with the Authority?
    `the prospectus or profile statement has been registered by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority registered the prospectus or profile statement, at the time of the dissemination?
    `the front page of the preliminary document contains the statement that it is a preliminary document subject to further amendments and completion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the front page of the preliminary document contain this statement: This is a preliminary document and is subject to further amendments and completion in the prospectus to be registered by the Monetary Authority of Singapore?
    `the front page of the preliminary document contains a statement in bold lettering that no offer or agreement may be made on the basis of the preliminary document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the front page of the preliminary document contain a statement in bold lettering that no offer or agreement may be made on the basis of the preliminary document to purchase or subscribe for any securities or securities-based derivatives contracts to which it relates?
    `the preliminary document contains or has attached to it a form of application that will facilitate an offer or the acceptance of an offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the preliminary document contain, or have attached to it, any form of application that will facilitate the making by any person of an offer of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts to which it relates, or the acceptance of such an offer by any person?
    `when the prospectus is registered the person takes reasonable steps to notify the persons to whom the preliminary document was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When the prospectus is registered by the Authority, do you take reasonable steps to notify the persons to whom the preliminary document was issued that the registered prospectus is available for collection?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F39 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(3) the person may disseminate the preliminary document without contravening subsection (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the person disseminates a preliminary document to any person` AND `the preliminary document has been lodged with the Authority`))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "disseminate a preliminary document which has been lodged with the Authority to any person"
        IF `the prospectus or profile statement has been registered by the Authority`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before a prospectus or profile statement is registered by the Authority"  -- SPLIT-SITE (ii)
        IF `the front page of the preliminary document contains the statement that it is a preliminary document subject to further amendments and completion` AND `the front page of the preliminary document contains a statement in bold lettering that no offer or agreement may be made on the basis of the preliminary document` AND (NOT `the preliminary document contains or has attached to it a form of application that will facilitate an offer or the acceptance of an offer`) AND `when the prospectus is registered the person takes reasonable steps to notify the persons to whom the preliminary document was issued`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person may ... without contravening subsection (1), if"  -- GRANT-RULING (1): an "if" gate failed on a function named for a power; the other reading is JUST FALSE

-- s 251(4)(a): oral or written material on a preliminary document. A "does not contravene" route with the same window and scope gates as subsection (3); the four conditions are joined by "and" (the "or" after (iv) joins paragraph (a) to paragraph (b)).
-- src:40544 | (4) Despite subsection (6), a person does not contravene
-- src:40545 | subsection (1) —
-- src:40547 | (a) by presenting, before a prospectus or profile statement is
-- src:40548 | registered by the Authority, oral or written material on
-- src:40549 | matters contained in a preliminary document which has
-- src:40550 | been lodged with the Authority, to any person if —
-- src:40552 | (i) the person states in the oral or written material (as the
-- src:40553 | case may be) that such matters are subject to further
-- src:40554 | amendments and completion in the prospectus to be
-- src:40555 | registered by the Authority;
-- src:40557 | (ii) the person states in the oral material, or in bold
-- src:40558 | lettering in the written material (as the case may be),
-- src:40559 | that no offer or agreement may be made on the basis
-- src:40560 | of such material to purchase or subscribe for any
-- src:40561 | securities or securities-based derivatives contracts to
-- src:40562 | which the material relates;
-- src:40564 | (iii) such material does not contain or have attached to it
-- src:40565 | any form of application mentioned in
-- src:40566 | subsection (3)(b); and
-- src:40568 | (iv) when the prospectus is registered by the Authority,
-- src:40569 | the person takes reasonable steps to notify the
-- src:40570 | persons to whom the material was presented that
-- src:40571 | the registered prospectus is available for collection;
-- src:40572 | or
@ref s 251(4)(a) (src:40544-40572)
GIVEN
    `the person presents oral or written material on matters contained in a preliminary document to any person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you present oral or written material, to any person, on matters contained in a preliminary document?
    `the preliminary document has been lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the preliminary document been lodged with the Authority?
    `the prospectus or profile statement has been registered by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority registered the prospectus or profile statement, at the time of the presentation?
    `the person states in the material that the matters are subject to further amendments and completion in the prospectus to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you state in the oral or written material that such matters are subject to further amendments and completion in the prospectus to be registered by the Authority?
    `the person states in the oral material, or in bold lettering in the written material, that no offer or agreement may be made on the basis of the material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you state in the oral material, or in bold lettering in the written material, that no offer or agreement may be made on the basis of such material to purchase or subscribe for any securities or securities-based derivatives contracts to which the material relates?
    `the material contains or has attached to it a form of application mentioned in subsection (3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the material contain, or have attached to it, any form of application mentioned in section 251(3)(b)?
    `when the prospectus is registered the person takes reasonable steps to notify the persons to whom the material was presented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When the prospectus is registered by the Authority, do you take reasonable steps to notify the persons to whom the material was presented that the registered prospectus is available for collection?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F39 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(4)(a) the person does not contravene subsection (1) by presenting the material` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the person presents oral or written material on matters contained in a preliminary document to any person` AND `the preliminary document has been lodged with the Authority`))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "oral or written material on matters contained in a preliminary document which has been lodged with the Authority, to any person"
        IF `the prospectus or profile statement has been registered by the Authority`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before a prospectus or profile statement is registered by the Authority"  -- SPLIT-SITE (ii)
        IF `the person states in the material that the matters are subject to further amendments and completion in the prospectus to be registered` AND `the person states in the oral material, or in bold lettering in the written material, that no offer or agreement may be made on the basis of the material` AND (NOT `the material contains or has attached to it a form of application mentioned in subsection (3)(b)`) AND `when the prospectus is registered the person takes reasonable steps to notify the persons to whom the material was presented`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person does not contravene subsection (1) ... to any person if"

-- s 251(4)(b): the eight kinds of person the material may equip. The text closes the list with "the following" and the purpose with "sole".
-- src:40594 | (i) a person licensed under this Act in respect of dealing
-- src:40595 | in capital markets products that are securities or
-- src:40596 | securities‑based derivatives contracts;
-- src:40598 | (ii) an exempt person;
-- src:40600 | (iii) a person who is a representative in respect of dealing
-- src:40601 | in capital markets products that are securities or
-- src:40602 | securities‑based derivatives contracts under this Act;
-- src:40604 | (iv) a representative of an exempt person;
-- src:40606 | (v) a person licensed under the Financial Advisers
-- src:40607 | Act 2001 in respect of advising on any investment
-- src:40608 | product;
-- src:40610 | (vi) an exempt financial adviser;
-- src:40612 | (vii) a person who is a representative in respect of
-- src:40613 | advising on any investment product under the
-- src:40614 | Financial Advisers Act 2001;
-- src:40616 | (viii) a representative of an exempt financial adviser.
@ref s 251(4)(b) (the eight persons) (src:40594-40616)
GIVEN
    `the person is licensed under this Act in respect of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person licensed under the Securities and Futures Act 2001 in respect of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the person is an exempt person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an exempt person?
    `the person is a representative in respect of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a representative in respect of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts under the Securities and Futures Act 2001?
    `the person is a representative of an exempt person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a representative of an exempt person?
    `the person is licensed under the Financial Advisers Act 2001 in respect of advising on any investment product` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person licensed under the Financial Advisers Act 2001 in respect of advising on any investment product?
    `the person is an exempt financial adviser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an exempt financial adviser?
    `the person is a representative in respect of advising on any investment product under the Financial Advisers Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a representative in respect of advising on any investment product under the Financial Advisers Act 2001?
    `the person is a representative of an exempt financial adviser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a representative of an exempt financial adviser?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 251(4)(b) the person equipped is one of the eight persons listed` MEANS
    IF `the person is licensed under this Act in respect of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` OR `the person is an exempt person` OR `the person is a representative in respect of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts under this Act` OR `the person is a representative of an exempt person` OR `the person is licensed under the Financial Advisers Act 2001 in respect of advising on any investment product` OR `the person is an exempt financial adviser` OR `the person is a representative in respect of advising on any investment product under the Financial Advisers Act 2001` OR `the person is a representative of an exempt financial adviser`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any of the following persons"

-- s 251(4)(b): material on a lodged prospectus, profile statement or product highlights sheet, for the sole purpose of equipping those persons, before registration.
-- src:40576 | (b) by presenting oral or written material on matters contained
-- src:40577 | in a prospectus, profile statement or product highlights
-- src:40578 | sheet which has been lodged with the Authority in respect
-- src:40579 | of an offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:40580 | contracts, before the prospectus or profile statement is
-- src:40581 | registered by the Authority, for the sole purpose of
-- src:40582 | equipping any of the following persons with knowledge
-- src:40583 | of the securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts in
-- src:40584 | order to enable the person to carry on the regulated activity
-- src:40585 | of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or
-- src:40586 | securities‑based derivatives contracts, or to provide any
-- src:40591 | financial advisory service in relation to the securities or
-- src:40592 | securities‑based derivatives contracts:
@ref s 251(4)(b) (src:40576-40592)
GIVEN
    `the person presents oral or written material on matters contained in a prospectus, profile statement or product highlights sheet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you present oral or written material on matters contained in a prospectus, profile statement or product highlights sheet?
    `the prospectus, profile statement or product highlights sheet has been lodged with the Authority in respect of an offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the prospectus, profile statement or product highlights sheet been lodged with the Authority in respect of an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the prospectus or profile statement has been registered by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority registered the prospectus or profile statement, at the time of the presentation?
    `the sole purpose is to equip a person with knowledge of the securities or contracts to enable the person to deal in them or to give financial advisory service in relation to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sole purpose of the presentation to equip a person with knowledge of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts in order to enable the person to carry on the regulated activity of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, or to provide any financial advisory service in relation to them?
    `the person equipped is one of the eight persons listed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(4)(b) the person equipped is one of the eight persons listed` answer for the person equipped? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F39 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(4)(b) the person does not contravene subsection (1) by presenting the material to equip those persons` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the person presents oral or written material on matters contained in a prospectus, profile statement or product highlights sheet` AND `the prospectus, profile statement or product highlights sheet has been lodged with the Authority in respect of an offer`))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "oral or written material on matters contained in a prospectus, profile statement or product highlights sheet which has been lodged with the Authority"
        IF `the prospectus or profile statement has been registered by the Authority`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before the prospectus or profile statement is registered by the Authority"  -- SPLIT-SITE (ii)
        IF (NOT `the sole purpose is to equip a person with knowledge of the securities or contracts to enable the person to deal in them or to give financial advisory service in relation to them`) OR (`the person equipped is one of the eight persons listed` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for the sole purpose of equipping any of the following persons"
        IF `the person equipped is one of the eight persons listed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the answer for the person equipped was not worked out

-- s 251(5): "To avoid doubt", a person may disseminate (a) a registered prospectus or profile statement, (b) a product highlights sheet that goes with one. No gate beyond what is described; the paragraphs are scope limits.
-- src:40620 | (5) To avoid doubt, a person may disseminate any of the following
-- src:40621 | without contravening subsection (1):
-- src:40623 | (a) a prospectus or profile statement that has been registered
-- src:40624 | by the Authority under section 240;
-- src:40626 | (b) a product highlights sheet in respect of which
-- src:40627 | section 240AA(1)(a) and (b) has been complied with and
-- src:40628 | which is disseminated with a prospectus or profile
-- src:40629 | statement that has been registered by the Authority under
-- src:40630 | section 240.
@ref s 251(5)(a) (src:40620-40630)
GIVEN
    `the document is a prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a prospectus or profile statement?
    `it has been registered by the Authority under section 240` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority registered it under section 240?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F40 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(5)(a) the person may disseminate the registered prospectus or profile statement` MEANS
    IF `the document is a prospectus or profile statement` AND `it has been registered by the Authority under section 240`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a prospectus or profile statement that has been registered by the Authority under section 240"

-- src:40626 | (b) a product highlights sheet in respect of which
-- src:40627 | section 240AA(1)(a) and (b) has been complied with and
-- src:40628 | which is disseminated with a prospectus or profile
-- src:40629 | statement that has been registered by the Authority under
-- src:40630 | section 240.
@ref s 251(5)(b) (src:40626-40630)
GIVEN
    `the document is a product highlights sheet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a product highlights sheet?
    `section 240AA(1)(a) and (b) has been complied with in respect of the sheet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has section 240AA(1)(a) and (b) been complied with in respect of the product highlights sheet?
    `the sheet is disseminated with a prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sheet disseminated with a prospectus or profile statement?
    `that prospectus or profile statement has been registered by the Authority under section 240` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority registered that prospectus or profile statement under section 240?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F40 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(5)(b) the person may disseminate the product highlights sheet` MEANS
    IF `the document is a product highlights sheet` AND `section 240AA(1)(a) and (b) has been complied with in respect of the sheet` AND `the sheet is disseminated with a prospectus or profile statement` AND `that prospectus or profile statement has been registered by the Authority under section 240`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a product highlights sheet in respect of which section 240AA(1)(a) and (b) has been complied with and which is disseminated with a prospectus or profile statement that has been registered by the Authority under section 240"

-- s 251(6)(a): the identifying statement. (i) for a business trust, (ii) in any other case ("where applicable" the underlying entity).
-- src:40641 | (a) a statement that identifies —
-- src:40643 | (i) in the case of an offer of securities or securities‑based
-- src:40644 | derivatives contracts being units or derivatives of
-- src:40645 | units in a business trust, the units or derivatives of
-- src:40646 | units, the person making the offer, the issuer, the
-- src:40647 | business trust and the trustee‑manager of the
-- src:40648 | business trust; and
-- src:40650 | (ii) in any other case, the securities, securities‑based
-- src:40651 | derivatives contracts, the person making the offer,
-- src:40652 | the issuer and, where applicable, the underlying
-- src:40653 | entity;
@ref s 251(6)(a) (src:40641-40653)
GIVEN
    `the offer is of units or derivatives of units in a business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts being units, or derivatives of units, in a business trust?
    `the statement identifies the securities or contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement identify the securities and the securities-based derivatives contracts (for a business trust, the units or derivatives of units)?
    `the statement identifies the person making the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement identify the person making the offer?
    `the statement identifies the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement identify the issuer?
    `the statement identifies the business trust and its trustee-manager` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement identify the business trust and the trustee-manager of the business trust?
    `there is an underlying entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an underlying entity (where applicable)?
    `the statement identifies the underlying entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement identify the underlying entity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 251(6)(a) the statement identifies what paragraph (a) requires` MEANS
    IF `the statement identifies the securities or contracts` AND `the statement identifies the person making the offer` AND `the statement identifies the issuer` AND (IF `the offer is of units or derivatives of units in a business trust` THEN `the statement identifies the business trust and its trustee-manager` ELSE ((NOT `there is an underlying entity`) OR `the statement identifies the underlying entity`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (a) says what the statement identifies and does not say what follows for a statement that identifies less

-- s 251(7): what satisfying subsection (6) takes. "must include all of the statements referred to in paragraphs (a), (b) and (c)" closes the gate; paragraph (d) is optional ("may include") and changes no answer.
-- src:40668 | (7) To satisfy subsection (6), the advertisement or publication must
-- src:40669 | include all of the statements referred to in paragraphs (a), (b) and (c)
-- src:40670 | of that subsection, and may include the statement referred to in
-- src:40671 | paragraph (d) of that subsection.
@ref s 251(7) (src:40668-40671)
GIVEN
    `what section 251(6)(a) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(6)(a) the statement identifies what paragraph (a) requires` answer for the statement? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the advertisement or publication includes the statement that a prospectus or profile statement for the offer will be made available when the offer is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the advertisement or publication include the statement referred to in section 251(6)(b): that a prospectus or profile statement for the offer will be made available when the offer is made?
    `the advertisement or publication includes the statement that anyone wishing to acquire the securities or contracts will need to make an application in the manner set out in the prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the advertisement or publication include the statement referred to in section 251(6)(c): that anyone wishing to acquire the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts will need to make an application in the manner set out in the prospectus or profile statement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 251(7) the advertisement or publication satisfies subsection (6)` MEANS
    IF (`what section 251(6)(a) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the advertisement or publication includes the statement that a prospectus or profile statement for the offer will be made available when the offer is made` AND `the advertisement or publication includes the statement that anyone wishing to acquire the securities or contracts will need to make an application in the manner set out in the prospectus or profile statement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "To satisfy subsection (6), the advertisement or publication must include all of the statements referred to in paragraphs (a), (b) and (c) of that subsection"

-- s 251(6): before registration, an advertisement that contains only the statements. The window is a split site (ii); "if it contains only the following" is a plain "if" (NOTHING when unmet).
-- src:40634 | (6) Before a prospectus or profile statement is registered, an
-- src:40635 | advertisement or publication does not contravene subsection (1) if it
-- src:40636 | contains only the following:
-- src:40641 | (a) a statement that identifies —
-- src:40643 | (i) in the case of an offer of securities or securities‑based
-- src:40644 | derivatives contracts being units or derivatives of
-- src:40645 | units in a business trust, the units or derivatives of
-- src:40646 | units, the person making the offer, the issuer, the
-- src:40647 | business trust and the trustee‑manager of the
-- src:40648 | business trust; and
-- src:40650 | (ii) in any other case, the securities, securities‑based
-- src:40651 | derivatives contracts, the person making the offer,
-- src:40652 | the issuer and, where applicable, the underlying
-- src:40653 | entity;
-- src:40655 | (b) a statement that a prospectus or profile statement for the
-- src:40656 | offer will be made available when the offer is made;
-- src:40658 | (c) a statement that anyone wishing to acquire the securities or
-- src:40659 | securities‑based derivatives contracts will need to make an
-- src:40660 | application in the manner set out in the prospectus or
-- src:40661 | profile statement;
-- src:40663 | (d) a statement of how to obtain, or arrange to receive, a copy
-- src:40664 | of the prospectus or profile statement.
@ref s 251(6) (src:40634-40664)
GIVEN
    `the prospectus or profile statement has been registered by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority registered the prospectus or profile statement, at the time of the advertisement or publication?
    `what section 251(7) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(7) the advertisement or publication satisfies subsection (6)` answer for the advertisement or publication? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the advertisement or publication contains only the statements in paragraphs (a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the advertisement or publication contain only the statements in section 251(6)(a), (b), (c) and (d)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F39 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(6) the advertisement or publication does not contravene subsection (1) before registration` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the prospectus or profile statement has been registered by the Authority`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before a prospectus or profile statement is registered"  -- SPLIT-SITE (ii)
        IF (`what section 251(7) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "To satisfy subsection (6), the advertisement or publication must include all of the statements referred to in paragraphs (a), (b) and (c) of that subsection"
        IF `the advertisement or publication contains only the statements in paragraphs (a) to (d)` AND (`what section 251(7) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an advertisement or publication does not contravene subsection (1) if it contains only the following"

-- s 251(8): after registration, an advertisement with the two statements, nothing beyond the prospectus, and the prescribed requirements. "complies with such requirements as the Authority may prescribe" is an input (a fact about the prescription).
-- src:40673 | (8) After a prospectus or profile statement is registered with the
-- src:40674 | Authority, an advertisement or a publication does not contravene
-- src:40675 | subsection (1) if —
-- src:40677 | (a) it includes a statement that the prospectus or profile
-- src:40678 | statement in respect of the offer of securities or
-- src:40679 | securities‑based derivatives contracts is available for
-- src:40680 | collection at the times and places specified in the
-- src:40681 | statement;
-- src:40683 | (b) it includes a statement that anyone wishing to acquire the
-- src:40684 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts will
-- src:40689 | need to make an application in the manner set out in the
-- src:40690 | prospectus or profile statement;
-- src:40692 | (c) it does not contain any information that is not included in
-- src:40693 | the prospectus or profile statement; and
-- src:40695 | (d) it complies with such requirements as the Authority may
-- src:40696 | prescribe by regulations made under section 341.
@ref s 251(8) (src:40673-40696)
GIVEN
    `the prospectus or profile statement has been registered by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority registered the prospectus or profile statement, at the time of the advertisement or publication?
    `it includes a statement that the prospectus or profile statement is available for collection at the times and places specified in the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the advertisement or publication include a statement that the prospectus or profile statement in respect of the offer is available for collection at the times and places specified in the statement?
    `it includes a statement that anyone wishing to acquire the securities or contracts will need to make an application in the manner set out in the prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the advertisement or publication include a statement that anyone wishing to acquire the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts will need to make an application in the manner set out in the prospectus or profile statement?
    `it contains information that is not included in the prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the advertisement or publication contain any information that is not included in the prospectus or profile statement?
    `it complies with the requirements the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the advertisement or publication comply with such requirements as the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F39 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(8) the advertisement or publication does not contravene subsection (1) after registration` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the prospectus or profile statement has been registered by the Authority`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "After a prospectus or profile statement is registered with the Authority"  -- SPLIT-SITE (ii)
        IF `it includes a statement that the prospectus or profile statement is available for collection at the times and places specified in the statement` AND `it includes a statement that anyone wishing to acquire the securities or contracts will need to make an application in the manner set out in the prospectus or profile statement` AND (NOT `it contains information that is not included in the prospectus or profile statement`) AND `it complies with the requirements the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an advertisement or a publication does not contravene subsection (1) if"

-- s 251(9)(a) to (h): eight kinds of advertisement or publication that do not contravene subsection (1). Each is a plain "if" route that answers JUST TRUE when met and NOTHING otherwise (fork F40); the combiner follows the eight.
-- src:40703 | (a) consists solely of a disclosure, notice or report required
-- src:40704 | under this Act, or any listing rules or other requirements of
-- src:40705 | an approved exchange or overseas exchange made by any
-- src:40706 | person;
@ref s 251(9)(a) (src:40703-40706)
GIVEN
    `it consists solely of a disclosure, notice or report required under this Act or any listing rules or other requirements of an approved exchange or overseas exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the advertisement or publication consist solely of a disclosure, notice or report required under the Securities and Futures Act 2001, or any listing rules or other requirements of an approved exchange or overseas exchange, made by any person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F40 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(9)(a) the advertisement or publication is a required disclosure, notice or report` MEANS
    IF `it consists solely of a disclosure, notice or report required under this Act or any listing rules or other requirements of an approved exchange or overseas exchange`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "consists solely of a disclosure, notice or report required under this Act, or any listing rules or other requirements of an approved exchange or overseas exchange made by any person"

-- src:40708 | (b) consists solely of a notice or report of a general meeting or
-- src:40709 | proposed general meeting of the person making the offer,
-- src:40710 | the issuer, the trustee‑manager of the business trust, the
-- src:40711 | underlying entity, the unitholders of the business trust or
-- src:40712 | any entity, or a presentation of oral or written material on
-- src:40713 | matters so contained in the notice or report at the general
-- src:40714 | meeting;
@ref s 251(9)(b) (src:40708-40714)
GIVEN
    `it consists solely of a notice or report of a general meeting or proposed general meeting of one of the persons named in paragraph (b), or a presentation of oral or written material on matters so contained in the notice or report at the general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the advertisement or publication consist solely of a notice or report of a general meeting or proposed general meeting of the person making the offer, the issuer, the trustee-manager of the business trust, the underlying entity, the unitholders of the business trust or any entity, or a presentation of oral or written material on matters so contained in the notice or report at the general meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F40 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(9)(b) the advertisement or publication is a notice or report of a general meeting` MEANS
    IF `it consists solely of a notice or report of a general meeting or proposed general meeting of one of the persons named in paragraph (b), or a presentation of oral or written material on matters so contained in the notice or report at the general meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "consists solely of a notice or report of a general meeting or proposed general meeting of the person making the offer"

-- src:40716 | (c) consists solely of a report about the issuer, the business
-- src:40717 | trust or the underlying entity that is published by the person
-- src:40718 | making the offer, the issuer, the trustee‑manager of the
-- src:40719 | business trust or the underlying entity (as the case may be),
-- src:40720 | which —
-- src:40722 | (i) does not contain information that materially affects
-- src:40723 | the affairs of the issuer, the business trust or the
-- src:40724 | underlying entity other than information previously
-- src:40725 | made available in a prospectus that has been
-- src:40726 | registered by the Authority, an annual report or a
-- src:40727 | disclosure, notice or report mentioned in
-- src:40728 | paragraph (a) or (b); and
-- src:40730 | (ii) does not refer (directly or indirectly) to the offer or
-- src:40731 | intended offer;
@ref s 251(9)(c) (src:40716-40731)
GIVEN
    `it consists solely of a report about the issuer, the business trust or the underlying entity, published by the person making the offer, the issuer, the trustee-manager of the business trust or the underlying entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the advertisement or publication consist solely of a report about the issuer, the business trust or the underlying entity that is published by the person making the offer, the issuer, the trustee-manager of the business trust or the underlying entity (as the case may be)?
    `the report contains information that materially affects the affairs of the issuer, the business trust or the underlying entity other than information previously made available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report contain information that materially affects the affairs of the issuer, the business trust or the underlying entity, other than information previously made available in a prospectus registered by the Authority, an annual report or a disclosure, notice or report mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b)?
    `the report refers directly or indirectly to the offer or intended offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report refer (directly or indirectly) to the offer or intended offer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F40 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(9)(c) the advertisement or publication is a report about the issuer, the business trust or the underlying entity` MEANS
    IF `it consists solely of a report about the issuer, the business trust or the underlying entity, published by the person making the offer, the issuer, the trustee-manager of the business trust or the underlying entity` AND (NOT `the report contains information that materially affects the affairs of the issuer, the business trust or the underlying entity other than information previously made available`) AND (NOT `the report refers directly or indirectly to the offer or intended offer`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "consists solely of a report about the issuer, the business trust or the underlying entity that is published by the person making the offer"

-- src:40736 | (d) consists solely of a statement made by the person making
-- src:40737 | the offer, the issuer, the trustee‑manager of the business
-- src:40738 | trust or the underlying entity that a prospectus or profile
-- src:40739 | statement in respect of the offer or intended offer has been
-- src:40740 | lodged with the Authority;
@ref s 251(9)(d) (src:40736-40740)
GIVEN
    `it consists solely of a statement, made by the person making the offer, the issuer, the trustee-manager of the business trust or the underlying entity, that a prospectus or profile statement for the offer or intended offer has been lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the advertisement or publication consist solely of a statement, made by the person making the offer, the issuer, the trustee-manager of the business trust or the underlying entity, that a prospectus or profile statement in respect of the offer or intended offer has been lodged with the Authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F40 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(9)(d) the advertisement or publication is a statement that the prospectus or profile statement has been lodged` MEANS
    IF `it consists solely of a statement, made by the person making the offer, the issuer, the trustee-manager of the business trust or the underlying entity, that a prospectus or profile statement for the offer or intended offer has been lodged with the Authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "consists solely of a statement made by the person making the offer, the issuer, the trustee-manager of the business trust or the underlying entity that a prospectus or profile statement in respect of the offer or intended offer has been lodged with the Authority"

-- s 251(9)(f) persons: the four kinds of publisher paragraph (f) excludes. Paragraph (e) refers to the same four.
-- src:40763 | (f) is a report about the securities or securities‑based
-- src:40764 | derivatives contracts which are the subject of the offer or
-- src:40765 | intended offer, published by someone who is not —
-- src:40767 | (i) the person making the offer, the issuer, the
-- src:40768 | underlying entity or (where the securities or
-- src:40769 | securities‑based derivatives contracts are units or
-- src:40770 | derivatives of units in a business trust) the
-- src:40771 | trustee‑manager of the business trust;
-- src:40773 | (ii) a director or an equivalent person of the person
-- src:40774 | making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or
-- src:40775 | (where the securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:40776 | contracts are units or derivatives of units in a
-- src:40777 | business trust) the trustee‑manager of the business
-- src:40778 | trust;
-- src:40783 | (iii) a person who has an interest in the success of the
-- src:40784 | issue or sale of the securities or securities‑based
-- src:40785 | derivatives contracts; or
-- src:40787 | (iv) a person acting at the instigation of, or by
-- src:40788 | arrangement with, any person mentioned in
-- src:40789 | sub‑paragraph (i), (ii) or (iii);
@ref s 251(9)(f) (the four persons) (src:40763-40789)
GIVEN
    `the person is the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or the trustee-manager of the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or (where the securities or contracts are units or derivatives of units in a business trust) the trustee-manager of the business trust?
    `the person is a director or an equivalent person of one of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a director or an equivalent person of the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or (for units or derivatives of units in a business trust) the trustee-manager of the business trust?
    `the person has an interest in the success of the issue or sale of the securities or contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have an interest in the success of the issue or sale of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the person acts at the instigation of, or by arrangement with, a person mentioned in sub-paragraph (i), (ii) or (iii)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person act at the instigation of, or by arrangement with, any person mentioned in sub-paragraph (i), (ii) or (iii) of section 251(9)(f)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 251(9)(f) the person is one of the four persons paragraph (f) names` MEANS
    IF `the person is the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or the trustee-manager of the business trust` OR `the person is a director or an equivalent person of one of them` OR `the person has an interest in the success of the issue or sale of the securities or contracts` OR `the person acts at the instigation of, or by arrangement with, a person mentioned in sub-paragraph (i), (ii) or (iii)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "someone who is not"

-- s 251(11): paragraphs (9)(e) and (f) do not apply when consideration or any other benefit is given for the publication.
-- src:40835 | (11) Subsection (9)(e) and (f) does not apply to an advertisement or
-- src:40836 | statement if any person gives consideration or any other benefit for
-- src:40837 | the publication of the advertisement or statement.
@ref s 251(11) (src:40835-40837)
GIVEN
    `any person gives consideration or any other benefit for the publication of the advertisement or statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does any person give consideration, or any other benefit, for the publication of the advertisement or statement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F40 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(11) subsection (9)(e) and (f) apply to the advertisement or statement` MEANS
    IF `any person gives consideration or any other benefit for the publication of the advertisement or statement`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (9)(e) and (f) does not apply to an advertisement or statement if any person gives consideration or any other benefit for the publication of the advertisement or statement"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply to an advertisement or statement if" says nothing of an advertisement for which none is given

-- src:40742 | (e) is a news report, or a genuine comment, by a person other
-- src:40743 | than any person referred to in paragraph (f)(i), (ii), (iii) or
-- src:40744 | (iv), in a newspaper, periodical or magazine or on radio,
-- src:40745 | television or any other means of broadcasting or
-- src:40746 | communication, relating to —
-- src:40748 | (i) a prospectus or profile statement that has been
-- src:40749 | lodged with the Authority or information contained
-- src:40750 | in such a prospectus or profile statement;
-- src:40752 | (ii) a disclosure, notice or report referred to in
-- src:40753 | paragraph (a);
-- src:40755 | (iii) a notice, report, presentation, general meeting or
-- src:40756 | proposed general meeting referred to in
-- src:40757 | paragraph (b);
-- src:40759 | (iv) a report referred to in paragraph (c); or
-- src:40761 | (v) a product highlights sheet;
@ref s 251(9)(e) (src:40742-40761)
GIVEN
    `it is a news report or a genuine comment, in a newspaper, periodical or magazine or on radio, television or any other means of broadcasting or communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the advertisement or publication a news report, or a genuine comment, in a newspaper, periodical or magazine or on radio, television or any other means of broadcasting or communication?
    `what section 251(9)(f) four persons answers for the person who makes the report or comment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(9)(f) the person is one of the four persons paragraph (f) names` answer for the person who makes the report or comment? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `it relates to one of the five matters in sub-paragraphs (i) to (v)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it relate to a prospectus or profile statement lodged with the Authority (or information in it), a disclosure, notice or report referred to in paragraph (a), a notice, report, presentation or general meeting referred to in paragraph (b), a report referred to in paragraph (c), or a product highlights sheet?
    `what section 251(11) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(11) subsection (9)(e) and (f) apply to the advertisement or statement` answer for the advertisement or statement? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F40 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(9)(e) the advertisement or publication is a news report or a genuine comment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`what section 251(11) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (9)(e) and (f) does not apply to an advertisement or statement if any person gives consideration or any other benefit"
        IF `it is a news report or a genuine comment, in a newspaper, periodical or magazine or on radio, television or any other means of broadcasting or communication` AND (`what section 251(9)(f) four persons answers for the person who makes the report or comment` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND `it relates to one of the five matters in sub-paragraphs (i) to (v)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is a news report, or a genuine comment, by a person other than any person referred to in paragraph (f)(i), (ii), (iii) or (iv)"

-- src:40763 | (f) is a report about the securities or securities‑based
-- src:40764 | derivatives contracts which are the subject of the offer or
-- src:40765 | intended offer, published by someone who is not —
-- src:40767 | (i) the person making the offer, the issuer, the
-- src:40768 | underlying entity or (where the securities or
-- src:40769 | securities‑based derivatives contracts are units or
-- src:40770 | derivatives of units in a business trust) the
-- src:40771 | trustee‑manager of the business trust;
-- src:40773 | (ii) a director or an equivalent person of the person
-- src:40774 | making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or
-- src:40775 | (where the securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:40776 | contracts are units or derivatives of units in a
-- src:40777 | business trust) the trustee‑manager of the business
-- src:40778 | trust;
-- src:40783 | (iii) a person who has an interest in the success of the
-- src:40784 | issue or sale of the securities or securities‑based
-- src:40785 | derivatives contracts; or
-- src:40787 | (iv) a person acting at the instigation of, or by
-- src:40788 | arrangement with, any person mentioned in
-- src:40789 | sub‑paragraph (i), (ii) or (iii);
@ref s 251(9)(f) (src:40763-40789)
GIVEN
    `it is a report about the securities or contracts which are the subject of the offer or intended offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the advertisement or publication a report about the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts which are the subject of the offer or intended offer?
    `what section 251(9)(f) four persons answers for the publisher` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(9)(f) the person is one of the four persons paragraph (f) names` answer for the publisher? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 251(11) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(11) subsection (9)(e) and (f) apply to the advertisement or statement` answer for the advertisement or statement? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F40 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(9)(f) the advertisement or publication is a report by a person other than the four` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`what section 251(11) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (9)(e) and (f) does not apply to an advertisement or statement if any person gives consideration or any other benefit"
        IF `it is a report about the securities or contracts which are the subject of the offer or intended offer` AND (`what section 251(9)(f) four persons answers for the publisher` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is a report about the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts which are the subject of the offer or intended offer, published by someone who is not"

-- src:40791 | (g) is a disclosure, notice, report or publication of a description
-- src:40792 | prescribed by the Authority, and such other conditions as
-- src:40793 | the Authority may prescribe are satisfied; or
@ref s 251(9)(g) (src:40791-40793)
GIVEN
    `it is a disclosure, notice, report or publication of a description prescribed by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the advertisement or publication a disclosure, notice, report or publication of a description prescribed by the Authority?
    `such other conditions as the Authority may prescribe are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are such other conditions as the Authority may prescribe satisfied?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F40 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(9)(g) the advertisement or publication is of a description the Authority has prescribed` MEANS
    IF `it is a disclosure, notice, report or publication of a description prescribed by the Authority` AND `such other conditions as the Authority may prescribe are satisfied`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "a disclosure, notice, report or publication of a description prescribed by the Authority, and such other conditions as the Authority may prescribe are satisfied"

-- src:40795 | (h) is a publication made by the person making the offer, the
-- src:40796 | issuer, the underlying entity or (where the offer is of units
-- src:40797 | or derivatives of units in a business trust) the
-- src:40798 | trustee‑manager of the business trust solely to correct or
-- src:40799 | provide clarification on any erroneous or inaccurate
-- src:40800 | information or comment contained in —
-- src:40802 | (i) an earlier news report or a genuine comment referred
-- src:40803 | to in paragraph (e); or
-- src:40805 | (ii) an earlier publication published in the ordinary
-- src:40806 | course of business of publishing a newspaper,
-- src:40807 | periodical or magazine, or of broadcasting by
-- src:40808 | radio, television or any other means of
-- src:40809 | broadcasting or communication, referred to in
-- src:40810 | subsection (10),
-- src:40812 | (h) provided that the firstmentioned publication does not
-- src:40813 | contain any material information that is not included in
-- src:40814 | the prospectus.
@ref s 251(9)(h) (src:40795-40814)
GIVEN
    `it is a publication made by the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or the trustee-manager of the business trust solely to correct or provide clarification on erroneous or inaccurate information or comment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the advertisement or publication a publication made by the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or (where the offer is of units or derivatives of units in a business trust) the trustee-manager of the business trust solely to correct or provide clarification on any erroneous or inaccurate information or comment?
    `the information or comment is contained in an earlier news report or genuine comment referred to in paragraph (e), or an earlier publication in the ordinary course of business of publishing a newspaper, periodical or magazine or of broadcasting, referred to in subsection (10)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the erroneous or inaccurate information or comment contained in an earlier news report or genuine comment referred to in paragraph (e), or in an earlier publication published in the ordinary course of business of publishing a newspaper, periodical or magazine, or of broadcasting by radio, television or any other means of broadcasting or communication, referred to in subsection (10)?
    `the publication contains any material information that is not included in the prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the publication contain any material information that is not included in the prospectus?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F40 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(9)(h) the advertisement or publication corrects or clarifies an earlier report or publication` MEANS
    IF `it is a publication made by the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or the trustee-manager of the business trust solely to correct or provide clarification on erroneous or inaccurate information or comment` AND `the information or comment is contained in an earlier news report or genuine comment referred to in paragraph (e), or an earlier publication in the ordinary course of business of publishing a newspaper, periodical or magazine or of broadcasting, referred to in subsection (10)` AND (NOT `the publication contains any material information that is not included in the prospectus`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is a publication made by the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or (where the offer is of units or derivatives of units in a business trust) the trustee-manager of the business trust solely to correct or provide clarification on any erroneous or inaccurate information or comment"

-- s 251(9): the combiner. Any one of (a) to (h) is enough. Only an answer JUST TRUE counts.
