-- src:40776 | contracts are units or derivatives of units in a
-- src:40777 | business trust) the trustee‑manager of the business
-- src:40778 | trust;
-- src:40783 | (iii) a person who has an interest in the success of the
-- src:40784 | issue or sale of the securities or securities‑based
-- src:40785 | derivatives contracts; or
-- src:40787 | (iv) a person acting at the instigation of, or by
-- src:40788 | arrangement with, any person mentioned in
-- src:40789 | sub‑paragraph (i), (ii) or (iii);
-- src:40791 | (g) is a disclosure, notice, report or publication of a description
-- src:40792 | prescribed by the Authority, and such other conditions as
-- src:40793 | the Authority may prescribe are satisfied; or
-- src:40795 | (h) is a publication made by the person making the offer, the
-- src:40796 | issuer, the underlying entity or (where the offer is of units
-- src:40797 | or derivatives of units in a business trust) the
-- src:40798 | trustee‑manager of the business trust solely to correct or
-- src:40799 | provide clarification on any erroneous or inaccurate
-- src:40800 | information or comment contained in —
-- src:40802 | (i) an earlier news report or a genuine comment referred
-- src:40803 | to in paragraph (e); or
-- src:40805 | (ii) an earlier publication published in the ordinary
-- src:40806 | course of business of publishing a newspaper,
-- src:40807 | periodical or magazine, or of broadcasting by
-- src:40808 | radio, television or any other means of
-- src:40809 | broadcasting or communication, referred to in
-- src:40810 | subsection (10),
-- src:40812 | (h) provided that the firstmentioned publication does not
-- src:40813 | contain any material information that is not included in
-- src:40814 | the prospectus.
@ref s 251(9) (src:40700-40814)
GIVEN
    `what section 251(9)(a) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(9)(a) the advertisement or publication is a required disclosure, notice or report` answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 251(9)(b) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(9)(b) the advertisement or publication is a notice or report of a general meeting` answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 251(9)(c) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(9)(c) the advertisement or publication is a report about the issuer, the business trust or the underlying entity` answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 251(9)(d) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(9)(d) the advertisement or publication is a statement that the prospectus or profile statement has been lodged` answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 251(9)(e) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(9)(e) the advertisement or publication is a news report or a genuine comment` answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 251(9)(f) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(9)(f) the advertisement or publication is a report by a person other than the four` answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 251(9)(g) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(9)(g) the advertisement or publication is of a description the Authority has prescribed` answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 251(9)(h) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(9)(h) the advertisement or publication corrects or clarifies an earlier report or publication` answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F40 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(9) the advertisement or publication does not contravene subsection (1) by being one of the eight` MEANS
    IF (`what section 251(9)(a) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 251(9)(b) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 251(9)(c) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 251(9)(d) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 251(9)(e) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 251(9)(f) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 251(9)(g) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 251(9)(h) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An advertisement or a publication does not contravene subsection (1) if it"

-- s 251(10): a newspaper or broadcaster that did not know and had no reason to suspect.
-- src:40818 | (10) A person does not contravene subsection (1) if —
-- src:40820 | (a) the person publishes any advertisement or publication in
-- src:40821 | the ordinary course of a business of —
-- src:40823 | (i) publishing a newspaper, periodical or magazine; or
-- src:40825 | (ii) broadcasting by radio, television, or any other means
-- src:40826 | of broadcasting or communication; and
-- src:40831 | (b) the person did not know and had no reason to suspect that
-- src:40832 | its publication would constitute a contravention of
-- src:40833 | subsection (1).
@ref s 251(10) (src:40818-40833)
GIVEN
    `the person publishes the advertisement or publication in the ordinary course of a business of publishing a newspaper, periodical or magazine, or of broadcasting by radio, television or any other means of broadcasting or communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you publish the advertisement or publication in the ordinary course of a business of publishing a newspaper, periodical or magazine, or of broadcasting by radio, television or any other means of broadcasting or communication?
    `the person knew or had reason to suspect that its publication would constitute a contravention of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know, or have reason to suspect, that its publication would constitute a contravention of section 251(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F40 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(10) the person does not contravene subsection (1) by publishing in the ordinary course of business` MEANS
    IF `the person publishes the advertisement or publication in the ordinary course of a business of publishing a newspaper, periodical or magazine, or of broadcasting by radio, television or any other means of broadcasting or communication` AND (NOT `the person knew or had reason to suspect that its publication would constitute a contravention of subsection (1)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person does not contravene subsection (1) if"

-- "authorised by this section" is not defined. It is read as: shown to be one of the nine routes in subsections (3) to (10) (fork F40). Only an answer JUST TRUE counts.
-- src:40457 | unless the advertisement or publication is authorised by this section.
@ref s 251(1) ("authorised by this section") (src:40457-40457)
GIVEN
    `what section 251(3) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(3) the person may disseminate the preliminary document without contravening subsection (1)` answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 251(4)(a) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(4)(a) the person does not contravene subsection (1) by presenting the material` answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 251(4)(b) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(4)(b) the person does not contravene subsection (1) by presenting the material to equip those persons` answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 251(5)(a) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(5)(a) the person may disseminate the registered prospectus or profile statement` answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 251(5)(b) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(5)(b) the person may disseminate the product highlights sheet` answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 251(6) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(6) the advertisement or publication does not contravene subsection (1) before registration` answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 251(8) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(8) the advertisement or publication does not contravene subsection (1) after registration` answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 251(9) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(9) the advertisement or publication does not contravene subsection (1) by being one of the eight` answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 251(10) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(10) the person does not contravene subsection (1) by publishing in the ordinary course of business` answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F40 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251 the advertisement or publication is authorised by this section` MEANS
    IF (`what section 251(3) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 251(4)(a) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 251(4)(b) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 251(5)(a) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 251(5)(b) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 251(6) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 251(8) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 251(9) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 251(10) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "authorised by this section" is not defined, and no route was shown to apply

-- s 251(12): the offence, and its penalty. "Any person who (a) contravenes subsection (1); or (b) knowingly authorises or permits" is the text's own limit.
-- src:40839 | (12) Any person who —
-- src:40841 | (a) contravenes subsection (1); or
-- src:40843 | (b) knowingly authorises or permits the publication or
-- src:40844 | dissemination of any advertisement or statement
-- src:40845 | mentioned in subsection (1),
-- src:40847 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:40848 | not exceeding $50,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:40849 | 12 months or to both and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a
-- src:40850 | further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day during
-- src:40851 | which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 251(12) (src:40839-40851)
GIVEN
    `what section 251(1) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 251(1) the person must not advertise the offer or publish the statement` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the person knowingly authorises or permits the publication or dissemination of an advertisement or statement mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you knowingly authorise or permit the publication or dissemination of any advertisement or statement mentioned in section 251(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F38 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(12) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF (`what section 251(1) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the person knowingly authorises or permits the publication or dissemination of an advertisement or statement mentioned in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who ... contravenes subsection (1) ... knowingly authorises or permits the publication or dissemination of any advertisement or statement mentioned in subsection (1) ... shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)

@ref s 251(12) (the penalty) (src:40839-40851)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 251(12) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 50000, 12, TRUE, 5000  -- a fine not exceeding $50,000, or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months, or both; a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

-- s 251(13): a flat negative. This section does not affect liability under any other law.
-- src:40855 | (13) This section does not affect any liability that a person has
-- src:40856 | under any other law.
@ref s 251(13) (src:40855-40856)
GIVEN
    `the liability arises under another law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the liability the person has arise under any other law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 251(13) this section affects a liability under another law` MEANS
    IF `the liability arises under another law`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not affect any liability that a person has under any other law"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any liability that a person has under any other law" says nothing of a liability under this Act

-- s 251(14): the Authority's exemption. The Authority's act is an input; the function answers JUST TRUE for a person or class it has exempted.
-- src:40858 | (14) The Authority may exempt any person or class of persons from
-- src:40859 | this section, subject to such conditions or restrictions as the Authority
-- src:40860 | may determine.
@ref s 251(14) (src:40858-40860)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has exempted the person, or a class of persons to which the person belongs, from this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority exempted the person, or a class of persons to which the person belongs, from section 251?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 251(14) the person is exempt from this section` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has exempted the person, or a class of persons to which the person belongs, from this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Authority may exempt any person or class of persons from this section"

-- s 251(15): the offence of contravening a condition or restriction under subsection (14), and its penalty. No imprisonment is stated.
-- src:40862 | (15) Any person who contravenes any of the conditions or
-- src:40863 | restrictions imposed under subsection (14) shall be guilty of an
-- src:40864 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:40865 | $50,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:40866 | exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day during which the
-- src:40867 | offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 251(15) (src:40862-40867)
GIVEN
    `the person contravenes a condition or restriction imposed under subsection (14)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you contravene a condition or restriction imposed under section 251(14)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F34 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(15) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes a condition or restriction imposed under subsection (14)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who contravenes any of the conditions or restrictions imposed under subsection (14) shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)

@ref s 251(15) (the penalty) (src:40862-40867)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 251(15) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 50000, 0, FALSE, 5000  -- a fine not exceeding $50,000; no imprisonment is stated (0); a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

@ref s 251(15) (the prohibition as a rule) (src:40862-40867)
GIVEN
    `the person` IS A Party @desc Who is bound by the condition or restriction?
    `the person is exempt under subsection (14) subject to a condition or restriction in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person exempt under section 251(14) subject to a condition or restriction that is in force?
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 251 action`
`s 251(15) the person shall not contravene a condition or restriction` MEANS
    IF `the person is exempt under subsection (14) subject to a condition or restriction in force`
    THEN PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `s 251(15) contravene the condition or restriction`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "a condition or restriction imposed under section 251(14) was contravened, which is an offence under section 251(15)"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 251(16): "publishing a statement" includes making one that is reasonably likely to be published. An "includes": not exhaustive.
-- src:40869 | (16) For the purposes of this section, any reference to publishing a
-- src:40870 | statement includes a reference to making a statement, whether oral or
-- src:40871 | written, which is reasonably likely to be published.
@ref s 251(16) (src:40869-40871)
GIVEN
    `the person publishes the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you publish the statement?
    `the person makes a statement, oral or written, which is reasonably likely to be published` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make a statement, whether oral or written, which is reasonably likely to be published?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 251(16) the person publishes a statement for the purposes of this section` MEANS
    IF `the person publishes the statement` OR `the person makes a statement, oral or written, which is reasonably likely to be published`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a reference to making a statement, whether oral or written, which is reasonably likely to be published"

-- s 251(17): "a statement" includes information presented in any form. An "includes".
-- src:40873 | (17) For the purposes of subsections (1) and (2), any reference to a
-- src:40874 | statement includes a reference to any information presented,
-- src:40875 | regardless of whether such information is in text or otherwise.
@ref s 251(17) (src:40873-40875)
GIVEN
    `the item is a statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the item a statement?
    `the item is information presented, whether in text or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the item information presented, regardless of whether it is in text or otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 251(17) the item is a statement for the purposes of subsections (1) and (2)` MEANS
    IF `the item is a statement` OR `the item is information presented, whether in text or otherwise`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "any reference to a statement includes a reference to any information presented, regardless of whether such information is in text or otherwise"

-- s 251(18): "affairs of the entity or the business trust" in subsection (2)(d). For a corporation it includes the matters in section 2(2); in any other case it is the matters the Authority prescribes ("is a reference to": a closed meaning).
-- src:40880 | (18) For the purposes of subsection (2)(d), the reference to affairs of
-- src:40881 | the entity or the business trust —
-- src:40883 | (a) in the case where the entity is a corporation, includes a
-- src:40884 | reference to the matters referred to in section 2(2); and
-- src:40886 | (b) in any other case, is a reference to such matters as the
-- src:40887 | Authority may prescribe.
@ref s 251(18) (src:40880-40887)
GIVEN
    `the entity is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity a corporation?
    `the matter is one of the matters referred to in section 2(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one of the matters referred to in section 2(2)?
    `the matter is one the Authority has prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one the Authority has prescribed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F42 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(18) the matter is within the affairs of the entity or the business trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the entity is a corporation`
        THEN (IF `the matter is one of the matters referred to in section 2(2)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "in the case where the entity is a corporation, includes a reference to the matters referred to in section 2(2)"
        IF `the matter is one the Authority has prescribed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any other case, is a reference to such matters as the Authority may prescribe"

-- s 251(18A): the three defined terms. "exempt financial adviser" and "financial advisory service" take their meanings from section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001, which this text does not contain.
-- src:40891 | (18A) In subsection (4) —
-- src:40893 | “exempt financial adviser” and “financial advisory service”
-- src:40894 | have the meanings given by section 2(1) of the Financial
-- src:40895 | Advisers Act 2001;
-- src:40897 | “representative” —
-- src:40899 | (a) in relation to dealing in capital markets products that
