    `the term has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person or service have the meaning that section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001 gives to "exempt financial adviser" or "financial advisory service"?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F42 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 251(18A) the term "exempt financial adviser" or "financial advisory service" is met` MEANS
    IF `the term has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "have the meanings given by section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001"

-- src:40897 | “representative” —
-- src:40899 | (a) in relation to dealing in capital markets products that
-- src:40900 | are securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:40901 | contracts under this Act or an exempt person, has
-- src:40902 | the meaning given by section 2(1); or
-- src:40904 | (b) in relation to advising on any investment product
-- src:40905 | under the Financial Advisers Act 2001 or an exempt
-- src:40906 | financial adviser, has the meaning given by
-- src:40907 | section 2(1) of that Act.
