§ `s 252: persons liable on a prospectus to inform the person making the offer`

-- s 252(1): the duty to notify. The duty arises for a person referred to in section 254(3) (other than paragraph (a)) who becomes aware, after registration and before the close of the offer, of (a), (b) or (c) where the failure to notify would be materially adverse to an investor. "as soon as practicable" carries no number, so the function says whether the notice was given as soon as practicable (a fact the person states); a duty whose gate is unmet answers NOTHING (fork F18).
-- src:40926 | 252.—(1) A person referred to in section 254(3) (other than
-- src:40927 | paragraph (a)) must notify in writing the person making the offer
-- src:40928 | of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts, as soon as
-- src:40933 | practicable, if the firstmentioned person becomes aware at any time
-- src:40934 | after the prospectus or profile statement is registered by the Authority
-- src:40935 | but before the close of the offer that —
-- src:40937 | (a) a statement in the prospectus or the profile statement is
-- src:40938 | false or misleading;
-- src:40940 | (b) there is an omission to state any information required to be
-- src:40941 | included in the prospectus under section 243 or there is an
-- src:40942 | omission to state any information required to be included
-- src:40943 | in the profile statement under section 246, as the case may
-- src:40944 | be; or
-- src:40946 | (c) a new circumstance —
-- src:40948 | (i) has arisen since the prospectus or the profile
-- src:40949 | statement was lodged with the Authority; and
-- src:40951 | (ii) would have been required to be included in the
-- src:40952 | prospectus under section 243, or required to be
-- src:40953 | included in the profile statement under section 246
-- src:40954 | (as the case may be) if it had arisen before the
-- src:40955 | prospectus or the profile statement was lodged with
-- src:40956 | the Authority,
-- src:40958 | and the failure to so notify would have been materially adverse from
-- src:40959 | the point of view of an investor.
@ref s 252(1) (src:40926-40959)
GIVEN
    `the person is a person referred to in section 254(3) other than paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person referred to in section 254(3), other than paragraph (a) of that subsection?
    `the person becomes aware after the registration but before the close of the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you become aware, at any time after the prospectus or profile statement is registered by the Authority but before the close of the offer, of any of the matters in section 252(1)(a), (b) or (c)?
    `a statement in the prospectus or the profile statement is false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a statement in the prospectus or the profile statement false or misleading?
    `there is an omission to state any information required to be included in the prospectus under section 243 or in the profile statement under section 246` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an omission to state any information required to be included in the prospectus under section 243, or in the profile statement under section 246, as the case may be?
    `a new circumstance has arisen since the prospectus or the profile statement was lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a new circumstance arisen since the prospectus or the profile statement was lodged with the Authority?
    `the new circumstance would have been required to be included had it arisen before lodgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the new circumstance have been required to be included in the prospectus under section 243, or in the profile statement under section 246 (as the case may be), if it had arisen before the prospectus or the profile statement was lodged with the Authority?
    `the failure to notify would have been materially adverse from the point of view of an investor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the failure to notify have been materially adverse from the point of view of an investor?
    `the person notified the person making the offer in writing as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you notify the person making the offer, in writing, as soon as practicable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F18 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 252(1) the person has notified the person making the offer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person is a person referred to in section 254(3) other than paragraph (a)`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person referred to in section 254(3) (other than paragraph (a)) must notify in writing the person making the offer"
        IF (NOT `the person becomes aware after the registration but before the close of the offer`) OR (NOT (`a statement in the prospectus or the profile statement is false or misleading` OR `there is an omission to state any information required to be included in the prospectus under section 243 or in the profile statement under section 246` OR (`a new circumstance has arisen since the prospectus or the profile statement was lodged with the Authority` AND `the new circumstance would have been required to be included had it arisen before lodgment`))) OR (NOT `the failure to notify would have been materially adverse from the point of view of an investor`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the firstmentioned person becomes aware at any time after the prospectus or profile statement is registered by the Authority but before the close of the offer that"
        IF `the person notified the person making the offer in writing as soon as practicable`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must notify in writing the person making the offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, as soon as practicable"

-- s 252(2): the offence of contravening subsection (1), and its penalty. A person contravenes the subsection when the duty arose and was not met (the function answers JUST FALSE).
-- src:40963 | (2) Any person who contravenes subsection (1) shall be guilty of an
-- src:40964 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:40965 | $50,000.
@ref s 252(2) (src:40963-40965)
