    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who contravenes subsection (1) shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)

@ref s 252(2) (the penalty) (src:40963-40965)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 252(2) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 50000, 0, FALSE, 0  -- a fine not exceeding $50,000; no imprisonment and no further daily fine is stated (0)

-- s 252(3): "a statement" in subsection (1)(a) includes information presented in any form.
-- src:40967 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1)(a), any reference to a
-- src:40968 | statement includes a reference to any information presented,
-- src:40969 | regardless of whether such information is in text or otherwise.
@ref s 252(3) (src:40967-40969)
GIVEN
    `the item is a statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the item a statement?
    `the item is information presented, whether in text or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the item information presented, regardless of whether it is in text or otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 252(3) the item is a statement for the purposes of subsection (1)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the item is a statement` OR `the item is information presented, whether in text or otherwise`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "any reference to a statement includes a reference to any information presented, regardless of whether such information is in text or otherwise"

